    "text": "{\n  \"anomaly_detected\": true,\n  \"confidence\": 0.99,\n  \"anomalies\": [\n    {\n      \"category\": \"bridged_nets\",\n      \"components\": [\"IC1\", \"L2\", \"U5\", \"J2\", \"U4\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"IC1.A2\", \"IC1.B2\", \"IC1.C1\", \"L2.2\", \"U5.28\", \"U5.29\", \"J2.4\", \"U4.2\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"BAT+\"],\n      \"observed\": \"The netlist places the regulator VIN, EN and FB pins, the inductor output, and the module, microSD and keyboard supply pins all on BAT+. The netlist has no +3V3 net. This conflicts with the specified arrangement of a regulated +3V3 output separate from BAT+.\",\n      \"expected\": \"BAT+ should feed IC1 VIN and EN; IC1 SW should connect through L2 to a separate +3V3 output, with FB and the 3.3 V loads on +3V3. The specification states: \u201cSW (pin B1) \u2192 L2 (1.0 \u00b5H) \u2192 +3V3 output rail\u201d and \u201cFB (pin C1) \u2192 +3V3 directly.\u201d\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"source\": \"netlist\",\n          \"quote\": \"(net (name \\\"BAT+\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"IC1\\\") (pin \\\"A2\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"IC1\\\") (pin \\\"B2\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"IC1\\\") (pin \\\"C1\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"J2\\\") (pin \\\"4\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"L2\\\") (pin \\\"2\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"U4\\\") (pin \\\"2\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"U5\\\") (pin \\\"28\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"U5\\\") (pin \\\"29\\\")\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source\": \"spec\",\n          \"quote\": \"SW (pin B1) \u2192 L2 (1.0 \u00b5H) \u2192 +3V3 output rail.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source\": \"spec\",\n          \"quote\": \"FB (pin C1) \u2192 +3V3 directly (fixed-output part; this is the standard connection for a fixed-voltage FAN53610 variant).\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source\": \"spec\",\n          \"quote\": \"+3V3 rail destinations: SKW92A module power pins (U5.28, U5.29) ... keyboard U4.2, microSD J2.4\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"The 3.3 V loads appear connected directly to BAT+, which also receives USB VBUS and barrel-jack power. They may therefore see raw battery or 5 V input rather than regulated 3.3 V, risking malfunction or damage; the regulator feedback and output are also connected to its input rail instead of a separate regulated output.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.99\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"An anomaly is present: the authoritative netlist merges the regulator output and intended 3.3 V loads onto BAT+, and contains no +3V3 net. This contradicts the specified regulated 3.3 V supply topology and could expose low-voltage components to raw input voltage.\"\n}",
